# @oxyfoo/* dependencies of the app come from the public npm registry, so the project installs
# without any account or token. Keep this line: the full avatar build is published under the same
# name and version on GitHub Packages, and a mapping of @oxyfoo to GitHub (e.g. in ~/.npmrc for the
# other OxyFoo projects) would otherwise lock it in package-lock.json for everyone.
# That build is fetched on demand by scripts/setup-avatars.js (see CONFIG.md).
@oxyfoo:registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
